# Knowledge and RAG

## Local-only memory (§4B.1)

- Ledger mirror, entity cards, and vectors live **100 % local**: SQLite + LanceDB under `<repo>/data/memory/`.
- **No cloud memory service** — do not add hosted vector DBs or sync prose to third-party memory APIs.

## Three planes — never collapse

| Question type | Store | Rule |
| ------------- | ----- | ---- |
| "What is the number?" | SQL master data / ledger | Authoritative; cite row id |
| "What do we know about X?" | Entity cards / confirmed facts | Only owner-confirmed facts are quotable |
| "Where is it written?" | Corpus chunks (BM25 + vector) | Citations only — **never** the source of a number |

Routing: number → SQL; know-about → card; where-written → retrieval; absent → **ASK**, never interpolate.

## Ingest bans

- Do **not** ingest Jarvis' own chat prose, tool error strings, or failed vision stubs as drawing or mail content.
- Vision error text is not a substitute for extracted drawing facts.

## Embeddings

- Record **embedding model id and dimension** per stored vector row; mixed dims in one index is invalid.
- Hash-of-words fallback (if present) must be labelled — not silently equivalent to ONNX embeddings.

## Writes

- Ingest runs off the hot request path (outbox/async where implemented); search reads must not block on unbounded ingest.

Skill `jarvis-architecture` / manifest §4B carries long retrieval procedures; this file states break-if-wrong constraints only.
